# Fingerprint-scoped, one line per finding. NOT a path or pattern exemption:
# each entry names a single file:rule:line, so any other secret — in this file
# or any other — is still caught.
#
# What these are: the cost corpus carries EVM token contract addresses, and a
# 42-character hex string scores high entropy, so the generic-api-key rule
# reads them as credentials. A contract address is public by construction. All
# four flagged lines are the same synthetic probe address,
# 0xabcdef0123456789… , added so one corpus case differs from its stored row in
# a hex LETTER — which is what makes it able to catch a missing lowercase fold.
#
# These entries will BREAK when the corpus is regenerated and the line numbers
# move. That is deliberate. A stale entry stops matching and the finding
# reappears, which is the safe direction to fail.
#
# A .gitleaks.toml allowlist was tried first and is NOT the answer. Scoped to
# this one path with condition = "AND", it silently disabled detection
# repo-wide: a planted high-entropy secret passed with the config present and
# was caught with it absent. Do not reach for that again without running that
# control both ways.
#
# The real fix belongs in the generator: a low-entropy letter-bearing address
# such as 0xaaaa…aaaa keeps the hex-letter property the mixed-case case needs
# and scores too low to trip the rule. Suggested to the monorepo; delete this
# file when it lands.
